<h1 align="center">🌐 TCP Unit Conversion System</h1>

<p align="center">
A lightweight multithreaded TCP client-server system built in Python that performs real-time unit conversions using a custom text-based protocol.
</p>

<p align="center">
Built with <b>Python sockets + threading</b> to simulate a simple distributed networked system.
</p>

---

## ⚙️ Features

- 🧵 Multithreaded TCP server — handles multiple clients concurrently using threads  
- 📡 Custom protocol design — structured CONVERT command format  
- 🔁 Real-time unit conversion engine — supports multiple categories  
- 🧪 Automated test suite — validates correctness + edge cases (21 tests)  
- 🖥️ Interactive CLI client — supports multiple simultaneous users  
- 📊 Server logging system — logs all connections, requests, and responses  

---

## 🧠 Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|------|------------|
| Language | Python 3.10+ |
| Networking | socket |
| Concurrency | threading |
| Architecture | TCP Client–Server |

---

## 📁 Project Structure

Server.py → multithreaded TCP server  
Client.py → interactive CLI client  
Tests.py → automated test suite (21 cases)  

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Check Python Version
```bash
python3 --version
Run Server
python3 Server.py

Server runs on:
0.0.0.0:5000

Host/port configured via HOST and PORT constants
Handles multiple clients via threading
Runs until Ctrl + C

On shutdown, connected clients are given a short grace window (~1.2s) before termination.

Run Client
python3 Client.py

Connects to localhost:5000 by default
Supports multiple simultaneous clients
Interactive terminal-based input

Run Tests
python3 Tests.py

Executes 21 predefined test cases
Covers valid inputs + error handling

🔄 Protocol Format

CONVERT <CATEGORY> <FROM_UNIT> <TO_UNIT> <VALUE>

Category	Units	Example
TEMP	C, F	CONVERT TEMP C F 25
LENGTH	KM, MI	CONVERT LENGTH KM MI 10
WEIGHT	KG, LB	CONVERT WEIGHT KG LB 5
CURRENCY	USD, CAD, EUR, GBP	CONVERT CURRENCY USD CAD 100

Case-insensitive commands supported
Use EXIT or QUIT to disconnect client

💬 Example Session

Enter request: CONVERT TEMP C F 25
Server response: RESULT 77.00 F

Enter request: CONVERT CURRENCY USD CAD 100
Server response: RESULT 137.00 CAD

Enter request: CONVERT FOO C F 25
Server response: ERROR Invalid category

Enter request: EXIT
Connection closed.

❌ Error Handling
Error Case	Response
Unknown category	ERROR Invalid category
Invalid unit	ERROR Invalid unit
Invalid numeric value	ERROR Invalid numeric value
Malformed request	ERROR Malformed request
📊 Server Logging

Client connected: ('127.0.0.1', 55842)
Request: CONVERT TEMP C F 25 → RESULT 77.00 F
Client disconnected: ('127.0.0.1', 55842)

⚠️ Known Limitations
Host/port are hardcoded constants (no CLI args)
Currency rates are static (no live API)
Assumes one request per TCP packet (recv simplification)
No authentication or encryption (educational use only)
No graceful shutdown messaging to clients
